# Decision procedures for trust-cg's e-graph rule statements (PKG-U6, PKG-U6b;
# README.md). Compiled in order by the pinned `lean -o`: trust-ir's SemR (the
# `semr` family's one copy), the rule vocabulary and the proof helpers of the
# `eqsat_rules` family (`from eqsat_rules`: this family holds no copy and
# changes neither), then the residue evaluator and what its outcome says of
# SemR's (`EqsatResidue`), the procedure `exhaust8` with its soundness theorem
# (`EqsatExhaust`), and what the procedure admits and refuses
# (`EqsatDecideControls`); then the three procedures of PKG-U6b, each with its
# soundness theorem and, after it, what it admits and refuses: `exhaust8p`
# (`EqsatPacked`), `bitwiseAll` (`EqsatBitwise`) and `ringAll` (`EqsatRing`).
# Each of the three imports `EqsatExhaust` and none imports another.
from semr SemR
from eqsat_rules EqsatRule
from eqsat_rules EqsatBasics
EqsatResidue
EqsatExhaust
EqsatDecideControls
EqsatPacked
EqsatPackedControls
EqsatBitwise
EqsatBitwiseControls
